The work-order log. Memory captures the note ("don't repeat this"); this log
names the PROMOTION TARGET — the exact file to edit so the cause cannot recur.
The two fields that do the work are Cause (which roots the fix) and Promotion
target (which file + what to change). See docs/05.

Attribution: classify every failure into exactly ONE cause before touching a file.
  skill-body      — right skill fired, its instructions were wrong/stale  → edit the SKILL.md body
  skill-trigger   — wrong skill fired, or the right one stayed silent      → edit the description: triggers
  skill-permission— wrong tool access (too broad or missing)               → edit allowed-tools / model frontmatter
  environment     — skill+trigger were fine, failure was external          → NOWHERE in the skill; log to ERRORS.md
-->

## [LRN-YYYYMMDD-NNN] <type> | <one-line rule>
- **Status:** pending | promoted | resolved
- **Cause:** skill-body | skill-trigger | skill-permission | environment
- **Summary:** <what happened and the durable rule it produces>
- **Promotion target:** <exact file + what to change>   (or `DONE: <the edit made>`)
- **Related:** <source memory file, e.g. feedback-some-lesson.md>

